{
  "beruf": "einzelhandel",
  "title": "Shops and supermarkets",
  "level": "A2–B1",
  "reviewed": false,
  "_note": "portuguese-for-work run, 2026-11-22: written by hand for Portugal (European Portuguese, pt-PT), not yet read by a human. translations.en = English meaning; deHint = German translation (the 'German' tab). Words already in the lexicon, the IMT deck or another sector are refs, with this job's own example and sense. Working conditions, contracts and rules are general orientation only.",
  "intro": "Supermarkets, shops and shopping centres are a common first job in Portugal: at the till, on the shop floor and in the stockroom. This deck has the till and the shop, the daily tasks, offers, exchanges and returns, safety, and what you say to customers and colleagues. Customers get the third person, usually with no pronoun: «Precisa de saco?», «Tem cartão de cliente?» Colleagues say tu.",
  "introEasy": "Do you work in a shop or supermarket in Portugal? Learn the words for your work here.",
  "jobs": [
    "Operador/a de caixa",
    "Repositor/a",
    "Empregado/a de loja",
    "Vendedor/a",
    "Talhante",
    "Padeiro/a"
  ],
  "tipps": [
    "At the till the questions are always the same: «Precisa de saco?», «Tem cartão de cliente?», «Quer contribuinte?» (the customer's tax number, NIF, on the receipt), «Paga com cartão?» Learn these first.",
    "Customers ask where things are: «Onde ficam os ovos?» Answer with the aisle: «No corredor cinco, ao fundo.»",
    "If you don't know, don't guess: «Só um momento, vou perguntar à minha colega.» For a complaint, call the chefe de secção; every shop must also have a complaints book (livro de reclamações)."
  ],
